  "reason": "Evidence: All three completed experiments use transformer aggregation, so we have no information on whether this structural choice is actually beneficial. The best config (config_013: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat, acc=0.599) establishes pca_n2000 >> scgpt and concat ≥ weighted as the current best settings. Question: Does transformer aggregation meaningfully outperform simpler avgpool aggregation when paired with the best-known RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion (concat)? This is the single most important untested structural variable in the current best configuration. Why this experiment: It isolates one variable (aggregation) from the current best config, directly tests whether the added complexity of a transformer is justified, and with 6 experiments remaining, resolving this question early prevents us from wasting budget on transformer-based variants if a simpler aggregation is equally effective or superior."
}

